tctiSH starts with a minimal Alpine Linux
environment, with few packages. You'll want to
add packages to get started. See the Alpine 
wiki for more details on using Alpine: 
<http://wiki.alpinelinux.org/>.

You can add packages using `apk add`. You can
search the available packages using `apk search`.

Examples:

	apk search clang
	apk add neovim

You can change this message in /etc/tcti_motd.

